1
00:00:03,030 --> 00:00:07,830
Two hundred "tests", each one is green;

2
00:00:07,848 --> 00:00:14,907
The finest score you've ever seen!

3
00:00:15,314 --> 00:00:17,997
My "tests"? I paste app code in haste—

4
00:00:18,007 --> 00:00:20,139
A perfect duplication!

5
00:00:20,149 --> 00:00:22,589
The sums agree! How sweet for me!

6
00:00:22,599 --> 00:00:24,899
(A shared miscalculation.)

7
00:00:24,909 --> 00:00:27,488
With screenshots, commas cause such dramas:

8
00:00:27,498 --> 00:00:29,717
A red notification.

9
00:00:29,727 --> 00:00:32,388
My "test"? Fantastic, automatic—

10
00:00:32,398 --> 00:00:34,646
I change its expectation!

11
00:00:34,656 --> 00:00:37,084
To boost my score, I cover more;

12
00:00:37,094 --> 00:00:39,444
They've trained me just to make the grade.

13
00:00:39,520 --> 00:00:42,053
Like kids in class, I aim to pass;

14
00:00:42,063 --> 00:00:44,044
The marks decide how tests get made.

15
00:00:44,054 --> 00:00:46,389
Did you actually test it?

16
00:00:46,399 --> 00:00:48,769
Press it, stress it, second-guess it!

17
00:00:48,779 --> 00:00:51,260
Find a clue? Congratulations!

18
00:00:51,270 --> 00:00:53,628
Now pursue its implications.

19
00:00:53,638 --> 00:00:58,139
What did you try? What did you find?

20
00:00:58,149 --> 00:01:01,010
What changed your mind?

21
00:01:03,826 --> 00:01:06,188
The gym? No net. We log a set;

22
00:01:06,240 --> 00:01:08,673
The app says "Saved!"— but what's in store?

23
00:01:08,683 --> 00:01:10,910
Reload the screen; no set is seen.

24
00:01:10,920 --> 00:01:13,359
Connect once more: still gone? Explore!

25
00:01:13,369 --> 00:01:15,937
We chase the clue; try something new:

26
00:01:15,947 --> 00:01:18,212
Connect, then save; the sets all stay.

27
00:01:18,222 --> 00:01:20,848
We drop the net, then save a set;

28
00:01:20,858 --> 00:01:22,990
A new check flags what went away.

29
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:25,201
Did you actually test it?

30
00:01:25,211 --> 00:01:27,593
Press it, stress it, second-guess it!

31
00:01:27,603 --> 00:01:30,031
Find a clue? Congratulations!

32
00:01:30,041 --> 00:01:32,382
Now pursue its implications.

33
00:01:32,392 --> 00:01:36,922
What did you try? What did you find?

34
00:01:36,932 --> 00:01:39,561
What changed your mind?

35
00:01:39,958 --> 00:01:42,460
A fresh bot crew? Here's what to do:

36
00:01:42,470 --> 00:01:45,025
Real browsers, a playbook, and users in mind.

37
00:01:45,035 --> 00:01:47,324
The goals you name will guide the game;

38
00:01:47,334 --> 00:01:49,803
Your oracles help them to judge what they find.

39
00:01:49,813 --> 00:01:52,113
One probes the chat— just me and Pat:

40
00:01:52,123 --> 00:01:54,658
Does Sam's new account show the text Pat just sent?

41
00:01:54,668 --> 00:01:57,013
One tests the cart, then hits restart:

42
00:01:57,023 --> 00:01:59,901
Do orders still match what the customer spent?

43
00:02:01,980 --> 00:02:04,455
We trade the news, compare the views;

44
00:02:04,465 --> 00:02:06,875
We share the doubts and observations.

45
00:02:06,885 --> 00:02:09,366
Some calls need you. We'll talk them through;

46
00:02:09,376 --> 00:02:11,818
We ask for fresh interpretations.

47
00:02:11,828 --> 00:02:14,416
A check applies a rule we've set;

48
00:02:14,426 --> 00:02:16,819
It tells us if that rule is met.

49
00:02:16,829 --> 00:02:19,188
To test, we ask what else— and why;

50
00:02:19,198 --> 00:02:21,755
Each clue can change what next we try.

51
00:02:21,765 --> 00:02:24,198
A check reports, "The sums agree!"

52
00:02:24,208 --> 00:02:26,607
We test: "Could both be wrong? Let's see!"

53
00:02:26,617 --> 00:02:29,039
The checks are part of how we test;

54
00:02:29,049 --> 00:02:32,282
We judge what serves the users best.

55
00:02:33,745 --> 00:02:36,191
Did you actually test it?

56
00:02:36,201 --> 00:02:38,658
Press it, stress it, second-guess it!

57
00:02:38,668 --> 00:02:41,136
Find a clue? Congratulations!

58
00:02:41,146 --> 00:02:43,569
Now pursue its implications.

59
00:02:43,579 --> 00:02:48,131
What did you try? What did you find?

60
00:02:48,141 --> 00:02:51,324
What changed your mind?

61
00:02:51,334 --> 00:02:54,196
It loses sets without the net;

62
00:02:54,544 --> 00:03:04,389
Who sees the logs? Not tested yet.
